  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1005 PM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nTuesday...\n\nThis will be the coolest and best chance for some precip over\nparts of the region. It will be noticeably cooler on this day,\nand the plains may not hit above 90 on this day. Northern El\nPaso county may see highs only in the U70s, with 80s over nearly\nthe rest of the plains. The San Luis valley will not see any of\nthe cooler air, and max temps around 90F are expected.\n\nThere will be a chance (scattered) of thunderstorms over the\nmtns/plains interface, especially east of the Sangre De Cristo\nmtns during the afternoon extending eastward to the vicinity of\nthe I-25 corridor. The remainder of the region will likely\nremain dry.\n\nTHere will be a non-zero chance of some locally heavy rain over\nthe Aspen Acres burn scar during Tuesday afternoon.\n\nWednesday, temps will warm up to around seasonable values on\nthis day. with mainly isolated storms possible region-wide\n(overall best chance will be down along the NM border region). \n\nGetting hot once again for Thursday. M90s most of plains with\naround 90F San Luis Valley. Isolated pops mainly over the plains\ndown along the NM border.\n\nFriday, U90s to 100F return to the plains with L90s San Luis\nvalley. Likely will be dry all areas.\n\nWeekend...\n\n100s plains and L90s SLV, dry all mainly areas.\n\nGuidance hints at the monsoon returning starting early next \nweek \\/Hodanish",
